        "created_at": "2021-12-16T03:22:00.839Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Many American Jews consider the “main” Hanukkah miracle to be the defeat of a powerful, well-organized, repressive force by a rebel militia. The Maccabees’ rededication of the temple, and the associated miracle of the lamp oil lasting long enough to get a proper resupply, is symbolically important but not what the holiday “revolves” around. The stories told, the songs, the dreidel game, and so on focus on themes like the struggle for freedom or holding on to your beliefs in the face of coercion. Here’s a good overview: <a href=\"https://medium.com/@mattsamberg/chanukah-explained-f70d97102453\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Chanukah, explained. It’s November, which means the “holiday… | by Matt Samberg | Nov, 2021 | Medium</a></p>",
